---
import Layout from '../../../../layouts/Layout.astro';import '../../../../styles/equipment.css';const d='/equipment/16-12/',slas='https://www.slas.org/SLAS/assets/File/public/standards/ANSI_SLAS_1-2004_FootprintDimensions.pdf',pitch='https://documents.thermofisher.com/TFS-Assets/LSG/brochures/EnduraPlate_96Well.pdf',ids=Array.from({length:96},(_,i)=>'ABCDEFGH'[Math.floor(i/12)]+(i%12+1));
---
<Layout pageTitle="General sample ware: dry indexing fixture" description="Move a rack of inert geometric markers without changing their well identity." wide={true}><article class="equipment" id="dryware"><nav class="eq-nav"><a href="/simulations/equipment/16-12/">← Equipment 16-12</a><a href="/simulations/equipment/">Register</a><a href="#ware-evidence">Reference sheet</a></nav><header class="eq-mast"><p class="eq-meta">16-12 / DRY SAMPLE IDENTITY</p><h2>Move the rack, not the well IDs</h2><p class="eq-lede">Place the slate marker in A1 (80 µL equivalent) and an amber marker in A2 (110 µL equivalent). Move the rack, then try adding 150 µL equivalent to A1. The two original entries should remain untouched.</p></header>
<div class="w-cols"><section><h3>Metric kit</h3><canvas id="ware-model" aria-label="Orbitable inert dry rack, 96-well plate, tubes and caps, glass vial and dish"></canvas><p id="ware-viewstatus" role="status">Loading metric GLB…</p><button id="ware-station">Whole kit / reset view</button><button id="ware-plate">Plate close-up</button><button id="ware-vials">Tube and vial close-up</button><p>Click any well in the plate view to select it. The lid and vial cap are also selectable.</p></section>
<section><h3>Dry placement</h3><p id="ware-selectedlabel"></p><div class="w-fields"><label>Well ID<select id="ware-selected">{ids.map(id=><option>{id}</option>)}</select></label><label>Inert label<select id="ware-label"><option value="slate">Slate</option><option value="amber">Amber</option><option value="sand">Sand</option></select></label><label>Dry geometric displacement, µL equivalent<input id="ware-volume" type="number" min="1" max="200" step="any" value="80"/></label></div><p><button data-well="A1">Select A1</button><button data-well="A2">Select A2</button><button id="ware-put">Place dry marker</button><button id="ware-move">Move rack</button><button id="ware-lid">Cover plate</button><button id="ware-cap">Park vial cap</button><button id="ware-reset">Empty and reset</button></p><p id="ware-pose"></p><p id="ware-status" role="status"></p><p>All examples are dry solid markers. No liquid, biological specimen, or handling protocol.</p></section></div>
<section><h3>Identity ledger</h3><div class="w-scroll"><table><thead><tr><th>Well</th><th>Label and sample IDs</th><th>µL equivalent</th><th>World center (mm)</th></tr></thead><tbody id="ware-ledger"></tbody></table></div><button id="ware-export">Download ledger JSON</button><p><a href={d+'example-ledger.json'}>Example export</a>. The JSON retains all 96 stable IDs, per-slot capacity and lineage, rack-relative and world coordinates, pose and revision history. Rejected placement leaves the prior fixture revision unchanged.</p></section>
<section id="ware-evidence"><h3>Reference, checks and reusable assets</h3><p>Original teaching plate with nominal 127.76 × 85.48 mm footprint from <a href={slas}>ANSI/SLAS 1-2004</a> and a 9 mm pitch, first well centers 14.38 and 11.24 mm from the relevant edges, cross-checked against the <a href={pitch}>Thermo Fisher EnduraPlate drawing</a>. No vendor part compliance is implied. Tube, vial, dish, lid, rack, well depth and usable 200 µL-equivalent capacity are original authored sizes, not measured product data. The kit stores one GLB well mesh and 96 named placements; the browser draws the wells as instances.</p><div class="w-cols"><figure><img alt="Original full dry labware kit rendering" src={d+'kit.webp'}/><figcaption>Original rack, plate, tube, vial, dish and removable lids; no liquids.</figcaption></figure><figure><img alt="Original plate render with dry markers in A1 and A2" src={d+'plate.webp'}/><figcaption>Original close-up of the independent dry markers in wells A1 and A2.</figcaption></figure></div>
<table><thead><tr><th>Check</th><th>Expected</th><th>Actual</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Move rack</td><td>52 mm X and 25 mm Z, no local slot drift</td><td>52 / 25 mm; local centers preserved</td></tr><tr><td>80 + 150 in A1</td><td>Reject above 200, original entries intact</td><td>A1 remains 80; A2 remains 110</td></tr></tbody></table><p><a href={d+'build-model.py'}>Editable Blender source</a> · <a href={d+'sample-ware.glb'}>Metric GLB kit</a> · <a href={d+'dry-ledger.mjs'}>Pure actions and schema</a> · <a href={d+'vr.json'}>VR ray targets and rack pose</a>. No headset check claimed.</p></section></article></Layout>
<script>import '../../../../lib/equipment/16-12/client.mjs';</script>
<style is:global>#dryware .w-cols{display:grid;grid-template-columns:minmax(0,1.1fr) minmax(0,1fr);gap:1rem}#dryware section{padding:1rem;border:1px solid var(--border);margin:1rem 0;min-width:0}#dryware :is(input,select,button){font:inherit;color:inherit;background:var(--panel);border:1px solid var(--border);padding:.45rem;max-width:100%;box-sizing:border-box}#dryware label{display:grid;gap:.2rem;min-width:0;margin:.35rem 0}#dryware label :is(input,select){width:100%;min-width:0}#dryware button{margin:.35rem .25rem .2rem 0;cursor:pointer}#dryware button:focus-visible,#dryware button[aria-pressed=true]{outline:3px solid #b28d5e}#ware-model{display:block;width:100%;height:330px;touch-action:none}#dryware figure{margin:.5rem 0}#dryware figure img{width:100%}#dryware .w-scroll{overflow:auto}#dryware table{font-size:.9rem;border-collapse:collapse;width:100%;text-align:left}#dryware td,#dryware th{border-bottom:1px solid var(--border);padding:.35rem}#dryware td{overflow-wrap:anywhere}@media(max-width:780px){#dryware .w-cols{grid-template-columns:minmax(0,1fr)}#ware-model{height:280px}}</style>
